cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OptiCommPy in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "OptiCommPy: Open-source Simulation of Fiber Optic Communications with Python"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Edson
    family-names: Porto da Silva
  - given-names: Adolfo
    family-names: Fernandes Herbster
abstract: >-
  OptiCommPy is a Python framework to simulate fiber optic communication
  systems, from the bits at the transmitter to the performance metrics at the
  receiver, including models of optical and optoelectronic devices, linear and
  nonlinear fiber propagation, optical amplification, receiver digital signal
  processing, forward error correction and performance metrics.
keywords:
  - optical communications
  - fiber optics
  - digital signal processing
  - simulation
  - python
